{
  "id": "T-293",
  "milestone": "M2",
  "depends_on": [],
  "title": "An autopilot job interrupted by a stop or restart runs its unfinished step again instead of blocking its task",
  "public_title": "Resume interrupted autopilot jobs from their breakpoint",
  "scope": [
    "bin/lib/fm_autopilot*.py",
    "bin/fm-autopilot.sh",
    "design/design.md",
    "tests/**",
    "design/tasks/T-293.json"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "Why. A stop or restart of the autopilot left the gate jobs of two tasks (T-278 and T-288) marked uncertain; the next step of each task (a replacement merge card, a review) never started, for hours, until firstmate fixed it by hand. Marking such a job done by hand hid the missing step (captain rule, 2026-10-11: an interrupted job is unfinished and resumes from its breakpoint, the step where it stopped).",
    "What, unfinished. A job that was running when the autopilot stopped is recorded as interrupted, never as done.",
    "What, resume. When the autopilot starts again and the job's pull request head is unchanged, it runs the same gate or protocol step again on that head, and the step that would have followed happens.",
    "What, partly acted. A job interrupted while the autopilot was acting on its result re-reads its saved result and finishes only the steps not yet done; each step it performs (raising a card, starting a review, recording a result) is idempotent by its id, so nothing is done twice.",
    "What, review. An interrupted review job is launched again only when no verdict was recorded and no reviewer is still running; otherwise the rule of one autopilot review per head stays as today.",
    "What, superseded. When the head has moved, the interrupted job is closed as superseded, the same way stale uncertain jobs are already closed today, and the autopilot handles the new head as usual.",
    "What, notices and old records. The 'Autopilot stopped during a child; reconcile its log' notice to firstmate (a wake) is no longer queued; on the first start after this change, an uncertain job whose notice is queued and not yet delivered is treated as interrupted and the notice is closed, while a job whose notice already reached firstmate stays uncertain for firstmate to finish.",
    "Docs. `design/design.md` §15.8 replaces the sentence that interrupted writes are reconciled, never rerun, with this behaviour.",
    "Done, tests. Tests show: an interrupted gate at an unchanged head runs again and its review starts (`autopilot: interrupted gate resumes`, fails on the base); a partly acted job finishes once (`autopilot: interrupted result acted on once`); an interrupted review with no verdict and no live reviewer is launched once (`autopilot: interrupted review relaunched once`); a moved head closes the job (`autopilot: interrupted job superseded`); an old uncertain job with an undelivered notice resumes and the notice closes (`autopilot: upgraded uncertain job resumes`).",
    "Out of scope. How a worker or reviewer round itself resumes after a crash; jobs that the autopilot did not start; jobs bound to the merge queue (the queue is off)."
  ],
  "explain": {
    "en": {
      "intent": [
